  "script": "The 1993 Toyota Supra Turbo greets you with its quad-headlight design, a signature look that complements its aggressive front fascia. Under the hood, the 1993 Supra Turbo boasts a 3.0-liter inline-six engine, with a commanding polished aluminum turbocharger, propelling this beast with 320 horsepower. The side view features an imposing rear wing, crucial for enhancing aerodynamics and emphasizing the Supra\u2019s performance intent. Inside, drivers find a five-speed manual shifter wrapped in leather, inviting them to command every bit of the car\u2019s power with precision. At the rear, the twin-tailpipe exhaust isn't just for show\u2014it's a statement of the Supra's turbocharged might. Designed by Isao Tsuzuki, this generation of Supra gained fame from its role in 'The Fast and the Furious,' solidifying its place in pop culture and among enthusiasts. Originally priced around $40K, these models have appreciated, with pristine examples fetching up to $85K today. So, would you choose the 1993 Toyota Supra Turbo for its iconic design, or is there another legend calling your name?",
